---
---

<section class="py-14 bg-gradient-to-b from-slate-900 via-slate-950 to-slate-900 text-white px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 border-y border-slate-800">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto">
    
    <div class="text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto mb-10">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-brand-500/20 text-brand-300 border border-brand-500/30 text-xs uppercase font-bold tracking-widest px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3">
        <span>🧪 Local Environmental & Geological Diagnostics</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-black tracking-tight text-white">
        Why Denton Homes Face Unique Plumbing Hazards
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-sm sm:text-base mt-2">
        Our plumbing solutions are specifically calibrated to withstand Denton County's mineral-dense municipal water and shifting clay sub-soils.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
      
      <!-- Hazard 1: Hard Water Scale Gauge -->
      <div class="bg-slate-900/90 border border-slate-800 p-7 rounded-2xl shadow-xl relative overflow-hidden flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div class="absolute -right-10 -top-10 w-40 h-40 bg-cyan-500/10 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>
        
        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">💧</span>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white leading-tight">Denton Municipal Water Hardness</h3>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-400">Sourced from Lake Ray Roberts & Lake Lewisville</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <span class="bg-rose-500/20 border border-rose-500/30 text-rose-300 text-xs font-black px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full uppercase">
              Hard Rating: 8.8 GPG
            </span>
          </div>

          <!-- Progress Bar Scale -->
          <div class="mb-5 bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
            <div class="flex justify-between text-xs text-slate-400 mb-1.5">
              <span>Soft (0-3.5 GPG)</span>
              <span>Moderate (3.5-7 GPG)</span>
              <span class="text-rose-400 font-bold">Denton (8.8 GPG)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="w-full bg-slate-800 h-3 rounded-full overflow-hidden flex">
              <div class="bg-emerald-500 w-1/4 h-full"></div>
              <div class="bg-amber-500 w-1/3 h-full"></div>
              <div class="bg-rose-500 w-5/12 h-full relative">
                <span class="absolute right-1 top-0 bottom-0 w-1 bg-white animate-pulse"></span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            High calcium and magnesium deposits settle at the base of water heaters in Denton subdivisions (like Southridge and Rayzor Ranch). This bakes into a hardened crust, suffocating heating elements and causing bottom tank corrosion within 6–8 years unless flushed annually.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-slate-800 flex items-center justify-between text-xs">
          <span class="text-brand-400 font-semibold">✓ Solution: Annual Descaling & Anode Inspection</span>
          <a href="/denton-tx/water-heater-repair/" class="text-white hover:text-brand-300 underline font-bold">
            Water Heater Options →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Hazard 2: Expansive Black Clay Soil -->
      <div class="bg-slate-900/90 border border-slate-800 p-7 rounded-2xl shadow-xl relative overflow-hidden flex flex-col justify-between">
        <div class="absolute -right-10 -top-10 w-40 h-40 bg-amber-500/10 rounded-full blur-3xl pointer-events-none"></div>

        <div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-4">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="text-2xl">🌍</span>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white leading-tight">North Texas Black Clay Soil Index</h3>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-400">High Plasticity Index (PI 42+) Foundation Movement</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <span class="bg-amber-500/20 border border-amber-500/30 text-amber-300 text-xs font-black px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full uppercase">
              High Slab Stress
            </span>
          </div>

          <!-- Soil Movement Scale -->
          <div class="mb-5 bg-slate-950 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-800">
            <div class="flex justify-between text-xs text-slate-400 mb-1.5">
              <span>Stable Sandy Loam</span>
              <span>Medium Expansion</span>
              <span class="text-amber-400 font-bold">Denton County Clay (Active)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="w-full bg-slate-800 h-3 rounded-full overflow-hidden flex">
              <div class="bg-emerald-500 w-1/4 h-full"></div>
              <div class="bg-amber-500 w-1/3 h-full"></div>
              <div class="bg-amber-600 w-5/12 h-full relative">
                <span class="absolute right-1 top-0 bottom-0 w-1 bg-white animate-pulse"></span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Denton County rests on active black clay soils that swell during wet spring rains and contract sharply in dry Texas summer heat. This constant foundation shifting bends rigid underground copper pipes, resulting in hidden sub-slab leaks and structural water loss.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="pt-4 border-t border-slate-800 flex items-center justify-between text-xs">
          <span class="text-amber-400 font-semibold">✓ Solution: Non-Invasive Acoustic Slab Detection</span>
          <a href="/denton-tx/slab-leak-repair/" class="text-white hover:text-amber-300 underline font-bold">
            Slab Leak Diagnostic →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>
